  "brief_description": "Christ kneels in prayer and looks up at an angel who holds a chalice. This is the beginning of the Passion (Christ's torture and crucifixion), when Christ prayed in the garden at Gethsemane: knowing that he is to die, Christ asks God to 'take this cup away from my lips'.\n\nIt was painted by Lo Spagna, an artist of Spanish origin who, after Raphael, was the most talented of Perugino’s associates. Lo Spagna – who spent most of his career in Southern Umbria - developed a sweet, charming yet idiosyncratic manner which distinguishes his paintings from the plethora of works produced in Perugino’s style.",
